   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ICBHI 2017 Challenge - Acoustic Feature Engineering & Benchmark Representation\n",
    "## Handcrafted Digital Signal Processing (DSP) Acoustic Biomarkers for Respiratory Auscultation\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides an in-depth interactive walkthrough of the **Phase 3 Feature Engineering Pipeline** for automated respiratory disease and adventitious sound detection using the **ICBHI 2017 Respiratory Sound Database**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Clinical Context & Motivation:\n",
    "- **Normal Breath Sounds**: Vesicular breathing characterized by broad, low-frequency acoustic energy (<500 Hz).\n",
    "- **Crackles (Râles)**: Discontinuous, explosive, non-musical adventitious sounds lasting <20 ms (fine crackles) or <100 ms (coarse crackles), typical of Pneumonia, Bronchiectasis, and heart failure.\n",
    "- **Wheezes (Rhonchi)**: Continuous musical/tonal sounds lasting >100 ms with dominant fundamental frequencies (typically 100–1000 Hz) caused by airway narrowing and airflow limitation, characteristic of COPD and Asthma.\n",
    "- **Both**: Co-occurrence of crackles and wheezes in a single respiratory cycle, common in severe obstructive/restrictive lung pathologies.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Acoustic Biomarker Taxonomy (307 Features):\n",
    "1. **Mel-Frequency Cepstral Coefficients (MFCCs)**: 20 coefficients + 1st Temporal Derivative ($\Delta$) + 2nd Temporal Derivative ($\Delta\Delta$), aggregated via Mean, Standard Deviation, Skewness, and Kurtosis across time frames (**240 features**).\n",
    "2. **Spectral Descriptors**: Spectral Centroid, Spread/Bandwidth, Rolloff (85% and 95%), Flatness, and Spectral Contrast across 7 octave sub-bands (**38 features**).\n",
    "3. **Temporal Dynamics**: Zero-Crossing Rate (ZCR), Root-Mean-Square (RMS) Energy, and Cycle Duration (**9 features**).\n",
    "4. **Tonal & Harmonic Descriptors**: Chroma STFT across 12 pitch classes (**24 features**)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import scipy.signal as signal\n",
    "import scipy.stats as stats\n",
    "import librosa\n",
    "import librosa.display\n",
    "import soundfile as sf\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n",
    "from sklearn.manifold import TSNE\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_selection import f_classif\n",
    "\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\", font=\"sans-serif\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.dpi'] = 150"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1. Load Extracted Feature Benchmark Datasets\n",
    "We load the structured feature matrices generated by `scripts/extract_features.py` adhering to the official ICBHI patient-independent benchmark split."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data_dir = \"../data/processed\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load train and test feature matrices\n",
    "X_train = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(data_dir, \"X_train.csv\"))\n",
    "y_train = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(data_dir, \"y_train.csv\"))\n",
    "meta_train = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(data_dir, \"metadata_train.csv\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "X_test = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(data_dir, \"X_test.csv\"))\n",
    "y_test = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(data_dir, \"y_test.csv\"))\n",
    "meta_test = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(data_dir, \"metadata_test.csv\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(os.path.join(data_dir, \"feature_names.json\"), \"r\") as f:\n",
    "    feature_meta = json.load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Total Handcrafted Features : {X_train.shape[1]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Train Set Dimensions      : {X_train.shape[0]:,} cycles x {X_train.shape[1]} features (Patients: {meta_train['patient_id'].nunique()})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test Set Dimensions       : {X_test.shape[0]:,} cycles x {X_test.shape[1]} features (Patients: {meta_test['patient_id'].nunique()})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total Benchmark Cycles    : {X_train.shape[0] + X_test.shape[0]:,}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display class distribution across splits\n",
    "summary_splits = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Train Count\": y_train[\"class\"].value_counts(),\n",
    "    \"Train %\": (y_train[\"class\"].value_counts(normalize=True)*100).round(2),\n",
    "    \"Test Count\": y_test[\"class\"].value_counts(),\n",
    "    \"Test %\": (y_test[\"class\"].value_counts(normalize=True)*100).round(2)\n",
    "})\n",
    "display(summary_splits)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. Feature Taxonomy & Breakdown\n",
    "The 307 handcrafted features span six complementary acoustic domains. We inspect the distribution of feature counts across each family."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "families = feature_meta[\"feature_families\"]\n",
    "fam_counts = pd.Series({k.replace('_', ' ').title(): len(v) for k, v in families.items()})\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 4))\n",
    "palette = sns.color_palette(\"Blues_r\", len(fam_counts))\n",
    "bars = ax.barh(fam_counts.index, fam_counts.values, color=palette, edgecolor=\"black\", linewidth=0.8)\n",
    "for bar in bars:\n",
    "    w = bar.get_width()\n",
    "    ax.text(w + 3, bar.get_y() + bar.get_height()/2, f\"{int(w)} features\", va='center', fontsize=10, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlim(0, max(fam_counts.values) + 30)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Number of Extracted Features\", fontsize=11, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Distribution of Handcrafted Acoustic Features by Domain\", fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Time-Frequency Feature Extraction Walkthrough\n",
    "We demonstrate step-by-step extraction on an exemplar cycle waveform: computing the log Mel-spectrogram, extracting 20 MFCC coefficients, and computing first and second temporal derivatives ($\Delta$ and $\Delta\Delta$)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load a sample cycle from raw database\n",
    "sr = 16000\n",
    "n_fft = 1024\n",
    "hop_length = 512\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create synthetic or exemplar cycle for demonstration\n",
    "t = np.linspace(0, 2.5, int(2.5 * sr), endpoint=False)\n",
    "# Synthetic normal breath with superimposed wheeze (tonal ~400 Hz) and crackle bursts\n",
    "sample_audio = 0.3 * np.random.randn(len(t)) * np.sin(2 * np.pi * 0.4 * t)**2\n",
    "# Superimpose wheeze harmonic\n",
    "sample_audio += 0.25 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * 380 * t) * (t > 0.8) * (t < 1.8)\n",
    "# Superimpose crackle clicks\n",
    "for click_t in [0.5, 0.9, 1.2, 1.5, 2.1]:\n",
    "    idx = int(click_t * sr)\n",
    "    sample_audio[idx:idx+40] += np.hanning(40) * 0.8\n",
    "\n",
    "# Normalize\n",
    "sample_audio = (sample_audio - np.mean(sample_audio)) / np.max(np.abs(sample_audio)) * 0.95\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute Mel-Spectrogram and MFCCs\n",
    "S_mel = librosa.feature.melspectrogram(y=sample_audio, sr=sr, n_fft=n_fft, hop_length=hop_length, n_mels=64)\n",
    "S_mel_db = librosa.power_to_db(S_mel, ref=np.max)\n",
    "mfcc = librosa.feature.mfcc(y=sample_audio, sr=sr, n_mfcc=20, n_fft=n_fft, hop_length=hop_length)\n",
    "d_mfcc = librosa.feature.delta(mfcc)\n",
    "d2_mfcc = librosa.feature.delta(mfcc, order=2)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot Multi-panel visualization\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(4, 1, figsize=(14, 10), sharex=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Waveform\n",
    "axes[0].plot(np.linspace(0, len(sample_audio)/sr, len(sample_audio)), sample_audio, color=\"#1864ab\", lw=1)\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Amplitude\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Exemplar Respiratory Cycle Waveform (Wheeze + Crackle Superposition)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Mel-Spectrogram\n",
    "img1 = librosa.display.specshow(S_mel_db, sr=sr, hop_length=hop_length, x_axis='time', y_axis='mel', ax=axes[1], cmap=\"magma\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Mel Freq (Hz)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Log Mel-Scale Spectrogram (64 Mels, 50-2000 Hz Bandwidth)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "fig.colorbar(img1, ax=axes[1], format=\"%+2.0f dB\", shrink=0.8)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. MFCC (Static)\n",
    "img2 = librosa.display.specshow(mfcc, sr=sr, hop_length=hop_length, x_axis='time', ax=axes[2], cmap=\"coolwarm\")\n",
    "axes[2].set_ylabel(\"MFCC Coeff\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[2].set_title(\"Mel-Frequency Cepstral Coefficients (MFCC 0-19)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "fig.colorbar(img2, ax=axes[2], shrink=0.8)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Delta MFCC (Velocity)\n",
    "img3 = librosa.display.specshow(d_mfcc, sr=sr, hop_length=hop_length, x_axis='time', ax=axes[3], cmap=\"viridis\")\n",
    "axes[3].set_ylabel(\"Delta MFCC\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[3].set_title(\"First Temporal Derivative ($\\\\Delta$ MFCC - Dynamic Velocity)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[3].set_xlabel(\"Time (seconds)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "fig.colorbar(img3, ax=axes[3], shrink=0.8)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4. Acoustic Biomarker Class Discrimination\n",
    "We visualize the distributions of key acoustic descriptors across the four sound classes (**Normal**, **Crackle**, **Wheeze**, **Both**) to inspect clinical separability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Combine X_train and y_train for visual exploration\n",
    "df_train_vis = X_train.copy()\n",
    "df_train_vis[\"class\"] = y_train[\"class\"].values\n",
    "\n",
    "key_biomarkers = [\n",
    "    (\"mfcc_00_mean\", \"MFCC 0 (Acoustic Energy)\"),\n",
    "    (\"mfcc_01_mean\", \"MFCC 1 (Spectral Balance)\"),\n",
    "    (\"spectral_centroid_mean\", \"Spectral Centroid Mean (Hz)\"),\n",
    "    (\"spectral_rolloff_85_mean\", \"Spectral Rolloff 85% Mean (Hz)\"),\n",
    "    (\"spectral_flatness_mean\", \"Spectral Flatness Mean\"),\n",
    "    (\"rms_energy_mean\", \"RMS Energy Mean\")\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(16, 9))\n",
    "axes = axes.flatten()\n",
    "palette = {\"Normal\": \"#2b8a3e\", \"Crackle\": \"#d9480f\", \"Wheeze\": \"#1971c2\", \"Both\": \"#7048e8\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "for idx, (col, title) in enumerate(key_biomarkers):\n",
    "    ax = axes[idx]\n",
    "    sns.boxplot(data=df_train_vis, x=\"class\", y=col, hue=\"class\", order=[\"Normal\", \"Crackle\", \"Wheeze\", \"Both\"],\n",
    "                palette=palette, ax=ax, width=0.5, fliersize=2, showcaps=True, legend=False)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=12, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"Value\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"Acoustic Biomarker Class Discrimination in Train Cohort (N = 4,142 cycles)\",\n",
    "             fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\", y=0.98)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5. Pairwise Feature Correlation & Multicollinearity\n",
    "Handcrafted acoustic features often exhibit inter-correlations (e.g. Spectral Centroid and Spectral Rolloff). We inspect the correlation matrix to understand feature redundancies and complementary representations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "corr_features = [\n",
    "    \"cycle_duration_feat\", \"mfcc_00_mean\", \"mfcc_01_mean\", \"mfcc_02_mean\",\n",
    "    \"mfcc_delta_00_mean\", \"mfcc_delta_01_mean\",\n",
    "    \"spectral_centroid_mean\", \"spectral_bandwidth_mean\",\n",
    "    \"spectral_rolloff_85_mean\", \"spectral_flatness_mean\",\n",
    "    \"spectral_contrast_b0_mean\", \"spectral_contrast_b3_mean\",\n",
    "    \"zcr_mean\", \"rms_energy_mean\", \"chroma_00_mean\", \"chroma_05_mean\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "corr_matrix = df_train_vis[corr_features].corr()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
    "mask = np.triu(np.ones_like(corr_matrix, dtype=bool))\n",
    "cmap = sns.diverging_palette(220, 20, as_cmap=True)\n",
    "sns.heatmap(corr_matrix, mask=mask, cmap=cmap, vmin=-1.0, vmax=1.0,\n",
    "            square=True, linewidths=0.5, cbar_kws={\"shrink\": 0.8}, ax=ax, annot=False)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Pairwise Pearson Correlation Matrix of Representative Biomarkers\", fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\", pad=15)\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45, ha='right', fontsize=9)\n",
    "plt.yticks(rotation=0, fontsize=9)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6. Unsupervised Manifold Learning: PCA & t-SNE\n",
    "We project the 307-dimensional acoustic feature space into 2D manifolds using Principal Component Analysis (PCA) and t-Distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding (t-SNE) to evaluate cluster separation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Sample 1,500 points for crisp visual clarity\n",
    "sample_idx = np.random.RandomState(42).choice(len(X_train), size=min(1500, len(X_train)), replace=False)\n",
    "X_sample = X_train.iloc[sample_idx]\n",
    "y_sample = y_train.iloc[sample_idx]\n",
    "\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_sample)\n",
    "\n",
    "pca = PCA(n_components=2, random_state=42)\n",
    "pca_res = pca.fit_transform(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "tsne = TSNE(n_components=2, perplexity=30, random_state=42, max_iter=1000)\n",
    "tsne_res = tsne.fit_transform(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 7))\n",
    "\n",
    "for cls_name, color in [(\"Normal\", \"#2b8a3e\"), (\"Crackle\", \"#d9480f\"), (\"Wheeze\", \"#1971c2\"), (\"Both\", \"#7048e8\")]:\n",
    "    mask = y_sample[\"class\"] == cls_name\n",
    "    axes[0].scatter(pca_res[mask, 0], pca_res[mask, 1], c=color, label=f\"{cls_name} (N={mask.sum()})\", alpha=0.6, s=25)\n",
    "    axes[1].scatter(tsne_res[mask, 0], tsne_res[mask, 1], c=color, label=cls_name, alpha=0.6, s=25)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(f\"PCA 2D Projection (Explained Variance: {pca.explained_variance_ratio_.sum()*100:.1f}%)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Principal Component 1\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Principal Component 2\")\n",
    "axes[0].legend(loc=\"upper right\")\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"t-SNE 2D Manifold Embedding (Perplexity = 30)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"t-SNE Dimension 1\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"t-SNE Dimension 2\")\n",
    "axes[1].legend(loc=\"upper right\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"Unsupervised Acoustic Feature Space Manifolds (Train Subsample)\", fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\", y=0.98)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 7. Supervised Feature Ranking: ANOVA F-statistic\n",
    "We calculate the one-way ANOVA F-score across all 307 features to identify the most statistically significant acoustic biomarkers distinguishing Normal vs. Adventitious respiratory sound classes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compute ANOVA F-score for binary task (Normal vs Adventitious)\n",
    "f_scores, p_vals = f_classif(X_train, y_train[\"is_adventitious\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "f_ranking = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Feature\": X_train.columns,\n",
    "    \"F_Score\": f_scores,\n",
    "    \"p_value\": p_vals\n",
    "}).sort_values(by=\"F_Score\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Top 15 Most Discriminative Handcrafted Acoustic Features:\")\n",
    "display(f_ranking.head(15))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Barplot of Top 15 Features\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "top15 = f_ranking.head(15)\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=top15, x=\"F_Score\", y=\"Feature\", palette=\"viridis\", ax=ax, edgecolor=\"black\", linewidth=0.7)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Top 15 Discriminative Biomarkers by ANOVA F-Statistic (Normal vs Adventitious)\", fontsize=12, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"ANOVA F-Score\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Feature Name\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8. Official Benchmark Split Verification & Dataset Audit\n",
    "We audit the official challenge split (`ICBHI_challenge_train_test.txt`).\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note on ICBHI Benchmark Structure*: In the official challenge partition, 124 of the 126 subjects are strictly patient-partitioned (zero leakage). Two multi-channel recording subjects (Patient 156 and Patient 218) were assigned across train and test by recording file in the challenge specification."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "train_patients = set(meta_train[\"patient_id\"].unique())\n",
    "test_patients = set(meta_test[\"patient_id\"].unique())\n",
    "overlap = train_patients.intersection(test_patients)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Number of Unique Training Patients: {len(train_patients)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Number of Unique Testing Patients : {len(test_patients)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Overlapping Patients in Challenge Split : {len(overlap)} -> {overlap}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verification of cycle total count\n",
    "total_cycles = len(X_train) + len(X_test)\n",
    "print(f\"Total Benchmark Cycles: {total_cycles:,} (Train: {len(X_train):,}, Test: {len(X_test):,})\")\n",
    "assert total_cycles == 6898, f\"Expected 6,898 cycles, found {total_cycles}\"\n",
    "print(\"VERIFICATION PASSED: All 6,898 cycles accounted for with 307 feature dimensions!\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
